    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "apt-get update succeeded — internet is available. Now I need to install gcc, make, and wget to fetch and compile SQLite.",
  "plan": "Install build-essential (provides gcc and make) and wget. Then download the SQLite amalgamation source. I'll run apt-get install with -y.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y build-essential wget 2>&1 | tail -15\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "apt-get install failed: not enough free space in /var/cache/apt/archives (101 MB needed). I need to check disk usage and free up space, or change the apt cache directory to a location with more space. /app may have space.",
  "plan": "Check disk free space. If /app has space, I can set the apt cache to /app (using -o dir::cache=... or a tmpfs). Simpler: clean apt cache and check df. Let me check df first to see where the space issue is.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -h / /app /var /tmp\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The filesystem reports 0 available space (100% used) despite 984G total, which suggests a quota/size limit on the overlay. The install needs 101 MB in /var/cache/apt/archives. I should clean the apt cache and any other reclaimable space, then retry. Let me check what's consuming space and clean up.",
  "plan": "Run apt-get clean to clear any partial downloads. Check current cache size. Then retry the install. If it still fails due to space, I'll redirect the apt cache to /app (which has the same but possibly less-restricted filesystem) or install only the minimal packages.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get clean; du -sh /var/cache/apt 2>/dev/null; df -h / | tail -1\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The filesystem shows 0 available with 955G used of 984G. The clean freed only a little. I need to find what's consuming space to free enough for the install, or find an alternative. Let me investigate disk usage by directory.",
  "plan": "Find large directories to free space. Check /usr, /var, /tmp, and look for large files. Then free space if possible. If the disk is truly at a hard quota, I may need to install a minimal compiler. First, investigate.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "du -sh /usr /var /tmp /opt /root /home 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Strange: df reports 955G used / 0 avail, but du finds only ~180M in major directories. This suggests either large hidden files or an inherited overlay quota. I need to find what's consuming space or verify if writing is actually blocked. Let me test disk write and search for large files.",
  "plan": "Test whether I can actually write ~50MB to /app. Also do a fuller scan for large files/directories (e.g., /var/lib, /var/cache bigger, or any huge files) to understand the space situation before deciding how to install gcc.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "dd if=/dev/zero of=/app/testfile bs=1M count=50 2>&1; ls -la /app/testfile; rm -f /app/testfile\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "du -sh /var/lib 2>/dev/null; find / -xdev -type f -size +50M 2>/dev/null | head\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Interesting: /app can clearly write 50MB (dd succeeded), yet df reports 0 available. This is a fuse-overlayfs df reporting quirk — apt's free-space check uses statvfs and sees 0, so it refuses. The real filesystem has space. I need to bypass apt's space check. Best approach: download the .deb packages manually with apt-get (which also checks, but I can set the cache dir), or better, retry since the cache was cleaned. Let me retry the install; if it still fails on space, I'll use apt-get download + dpkg.",
  "plan": "Retry apt-get install. If it still fails due to the bogus free-space estimate, I'll point apt's cache to /app and/or use `apt-get download` then `dpkg -i`. First just retry to confirm behavior.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y build-essential wget 2>&1 | tail -8\n",
      "duration": 30.0
    }
  ]
}

